§§ `s.3(a): the prohibition as a regulative rule`

-- Work without a licence: the person is prohibited, and doing the work is the breach.
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s07` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 5
-- EXPECT: BREACH
-- Work with the appropriate licence: no prohibition arises.
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s01` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 5
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
-- The prohibition stands for the life of the licence situation: no period is stated, so it does not sunset.
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s03` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s03` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 400
-- EXPECT: BREACH
-- Outside the conditions of a licence of the right kind: also a breach of s.3(a).
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s29` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 1
-- EXPECT: BREACH
-- The Law not yet in force for the work, or an exempted class: no prohibition arises.
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s27` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 1
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` `work s28` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `do work on a cooling system` AT 1
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED

§§ `s.3(b): the exemption order`

`an order made after full consultation and satisfaction` MEANS `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS TRUE
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS TRUE

`an order without consultation` MEANS `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
    `the Council was consulted` IS FALSE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS FALSE
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS TRUE
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS TRUE

`an order after a consultation whose advice was not valid` MEANS `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS FALSE
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS TRUE
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS TRUE

`an order without the Minister's satisfaction` MEANS `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS FALSE
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS TRUE

`an order that fixes conditions but determines no exemption` MEANS `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS TRUE
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` `an order made after full consultation and satisfaction`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` `an order without consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` `an order after a consultation whose advice was not valid`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` `an order without the Minister's satisfaction`
#ASSERT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order, a consultation counting once held` `an order made after full consultation and satisfaction`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order, a consultation counting once held` `an order without consultation`
#ASSERT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order, a consultation counting once held` `an order after a consultation whose advice was not valid`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order, a consultation counting once held` `an order without the Minister's satisfaction`
#ASSERT `the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` `an order made after full consultation and satisfaction`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` `an order that fixes conditions but determines no exemption`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` `an order without consultation`
-- The power exercised: FULFILLED.  Unexercised, the permission stands.  Where its preconditions are missing, no permission arises.
